### Remaining Concerns (your call)
1. **The Cameo marathon is still told twice.** I removed the duplicated payoff, but "500 personalized videos at $100" appears verbatim in both the intro and the founding section. ~1,500 words apart, so it may be a deliberate restatement. Cutting the numbers from one would buy back ~8 words of headroom.
2. **The business anomaly is raised in the body and resolved only in the accordion.** "Somebody in that building is very good at saying no. Nothing on the record establishes that it is her" is a live question the body never returns to; the rabbit hole answers it, but most readers won't open it. That's a genuine orphaned thread — either let the body concede it in a clause, or accept that the TL;DR promise ("the thing the type does not explain") is redeemed only for the nerds.
3. **Chronology takes one bump at section 5.** The piece runs 2019→2024 (founding), then jumps to present-tense adult complaint, then back to Feb 2023 (Jules). It works because the complaint section is timeless, but a date-tracking reader feels it. Fixable only by reordering, which is a bigger call than a cohesion pass should make.
